From d73f4fd0a182149926b82b1cccd8a623c5b653d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:43:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: HDMI VRR left off in the mode set of an HDR10+
 video on Turing and Ampere

On Turing and Ampere the SOR has one slot for an InfoFrame of a client
next to the HDR one, the generic InfoFrame slot, where HDR10+ goes.
NVKMS turns HDMI VRR on in every mode set of a display that declares it,
from 50 Hz and 720 lines up, and then sends the EMP of HDMI VRR in that
slot every frame whether flips use VRR or not, so HDR10+ was refused at
50 and 60 Hz on such a display. Kodi never flips with VRR.

nvidia-drm gives those connectors NV_HDMI_VRR_OFF
(nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9051): with 1 the mode set asks NVKMS for no
Adaptive-Sync and no EMP goes out. Kodi sets it only in the commit of
the mode of a video that the hold of its change of mode releases, which
is a mode set anyway, and only where it stands between the video and
HDR10+: the property is there, the video sends HDR10+ that the display
takes (a payload of a version it takes, or Dolby Vision sent as HDR10+),
the display declares HDMI VRR, and the mode has 720 lines or more at
50 Hz or more (CHdmiVrrOff::Wanted()). Never a change of mode for it.
Any other mode set puts it back to 0, the GUI's after the video among
them (CHdmiVrrOff::Stage()). A test of the request that fails with it is
made again without it and without the HDR10+ payload, so that the video
goes out as it did before, as HDR10; kodi.log says which it was.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/HdmiVrrOff.h              | 112 +++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp          |  67 +++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h            |  10 ++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h |   3 +
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMAtomic.cpp         |  17 ++-
 5 files changed, 207 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/windowing/gbm/HdmiVrrOff.h

